; SELinux domain for cella-gateway: the membrane. Its whole interface
; is one machine's directory (1.6.13): write on verdict, valve, and
; audit; read on ledger and pid; no exec anywhere, ever. Bound to
; that one machine's category.
;
; No seccomp/bwrap profile placeholder exists yet for cella-gateway
; under security/profiles/cella-gateway/ as of this lane's build --
; lane a's scaffold covers eight personas and this crate is a ninth;
; flagged in the shakedown report, not decided here.
(type cella_gateway_t)
(type cella_gateway_exec_t)
(call cella_domain (cella_gateway_t cella_gateway_exec_t))
(typeattributeset mcs_constrained_type (cella_gateway_t))

(allow cella_gateway_t cella_machine_data_t (dir (read search getattr)))
; verdict, valve, and audit take write; ledger and pid take read --
; both collapse to one type-enforcement rule here, since the five
; files share cella_machine_data_t and SELinux does not see
; filenames. Splitting them into distinct per-file types so the
; verb's own read/write split becomes a real MAC boundary, not just
; the gateway code's discipline, is future work, named here rather
; than assumed.
(allow cella_gateway_t cella_machine_data_t (file (read write open getattr)))
